From 9b7022fa7f0e0f47f28b466edfc17bd0337e12b6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: local <local@example.invalid>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 12:02:11 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 07/34] WP31: Exactly one automatic resend per interrupted
 filing

Bug found during integration: when the sweep's one automatic resend of an
interrupted (crash or timeout) batch came back unclear too, the resend was a
new outcome_unknown batch with retried_at empty, so the next sweep resent it
again. The resend repeated every sweep for as long as UbyPort timed out.

Owner decision Q4: one automatic retry, then hold and alert the host.

- reporting._retry_outcome_unknown_batches sends the resend with
  submission.mode = 'auto_resend' (reporting.AUTO_RESEND_MODE) and never
  resends a batch with that mode. The mode is written when the resend's row
  is inserted, so a resend cut off by a crash is not resent either.
- An unclear resend stays outcome_unknown: its guests stay in doubt, out of
  the sweep, and the existing submission_outcome_unknown alert and mail fire
  for it. No schema change.
- A send by the host (manual, ignore_automation) is still allowed and is not
  the automatic one: if its own answer is unclear, the sweep resends it once.
- Unchanged: claim_sendable as the only double-filing guard, the in-doubt
  filter, and duplicate answer 150 counting as filed.
- Reports show the new mode: reports.mode.auto_resend (EN, CS).

Tests (tests/test_stale_submission.py): a crashed filing is resent once; an
unclear resend is not resent over three sweeps, the guest stays held and the
host is alerted and mailed once; a crash during the resend is not resent;
a manual send afterwards files the guest and clears the alert; an unclear
manual send gets one automatic resend; an accepted or duplicate (150) resend
resolves everything. The WP23 watchdog test for such a stay is added with
WP23. test_host_labels lists the new mode.
